From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:33:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] phi: kernel instantiation and type registry for MinGW

- GCC must explicitly instantiate kernels in PD_REGISTER_* (as on Linux):
  at -O3 the instances are otherwise never emitted for other TUs.
- The MSVC-only exported instantiations (template PADDLE_API void
  XKernel<...>) become dllexport explicit instantiation declarations on
  MinGW (PD_WIN_KERNEL_INSTANTIATION) so the registration defines them.
- TypeRegistry<Base> was instantiated per DLL from its header, so type
  ids registered in phi.dll and libpaddle.pyd collided and
  TypeInfoTraits::classof() misidentified tensors (crash in
  Tensor.dtype); instantiate it once in phi.
---
